{"componentChunkName":"component---src-pages-markdown-remark-frontmatter-slug-js","path":"/projects/posterior-aware-pd-phenotyping/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<h1>Posterior-Aware Motor Phenotyping with Multimodal Imaging Validation in Parkinson's Disease</h1>\n<p><strong>Harsh Milind Tirhekar, Priyanshi Yadav, Chandrajit Bajaj</strong></p>\n<p>Department of Computer Science, The University of Texas at Austin</p>\n<p>Department of Biomedical Engineering, National Institute of Technology Raipur</p>\n<p>Oden Institute for Computational Engineering and Sciences, The University of Texas at Austin</p>\n<p><strong>bioRxiv / MICCAI 2026</strong>   |   <a href=\"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.06.12.732003v1.full.pdf\">Paper</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/5b6ee/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 56.49999999999999%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Posterior-aware motor-state phenotyping graphical abstract' title='' src='/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/5a190/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png' srcset='/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/772e8/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png 200w,\n/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/e17e5/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png 400w,\n/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/5a190/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png 800w,\n/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/c1b63/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png 1200w,\n/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/29007/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png 1600w,\n/static/96db8253bbaf9557406dcf8524c3421c/5b6ee/fig1_motor_state_graphical_abstract.png 1672w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 1.</strong> Posterior-aware motor-state phenotyping concept. Longitudinal MDS-UPDRS-III motor assessments are represented as soft posterior profiles over motor states, then interpreted through patient-level phenotype families and imaging-associated validation with DaTSCAN SBR and structural MRI / FreeSurfer ROIs.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>TL;DR</h3>\n<p>This work builds a posterior-aware Bayesian Gaussian mixture modeling framework for Parkinson's disease motor phenotyping. Instead of assigning each visit to a hard subtype, the model keeps the full posterior state vector, allowing high-confidence, boundary, and mixed motor-state presentations to be distinguished. The resulting five-state visit-level representation is then validated against DaTSCAN striatal binding ratios, FreeSurfer structural MRI volumes, and transfer to BioFIND without refitting.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Why this matters</h3>\n<p>Two patients can have similar total MDS-UPDRS-III burden while expressing very different motor profiles. One may be tremor-weighted, another axial-weighted, and another mixed across rigidity, bradykinesia, axial, tremor, and bulbar domains. Hard subtype labels lose that uncertainty.</p>\n<p>The paper's central point is that posterior probabilities are useful, not incidental. They identify visits that are clearly assigned, visits that sit near motor-state boundaries, and patient trajectories that can shift over follow-up. The imaging analyses then test whether these motor-state assignments have complementary biological correlates rather than treating the clusters as purely clinical artifacts.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Framework</h3>\n<p>The MICCAI study analyzes 29,366 longitudinal MDS-UPDRS-III assessments from 1,847 PPMI participants. The item-level motor exam is aggregated into five clinical domains: tremor, bradykinesia, rigidity, axial function, and bulbar symptoms.</p>\n<p>A predefined Bayesian Gaussian mixture model search over 2,912 configurations selects a five-state representation. The framework uses model-conditioned posterior vectors to classify visits as high-confidence textbook assignments or intermediate-confidence chimera assignments. It also reconciles five-state and eight-state views through strong cross-granularity nesting.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/9dd22/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 29.500000000000004%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Posterior-aware phenotyping pipeline from the paper' title='' src='/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/5a190/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png' srcset='/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/772e8/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png 200w,\n/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/e17e5/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png 400w,\n/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/5a190/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png 800w,\n/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/c1b63/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png 1200w,\n/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/29007/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png 1600w,\n/static/5b272930c4eb7a3e1c262b40b6a830e3/9dd22/fig2_posterior_pipeline.png 4540w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 2.</strong> Posterior-aware phenotyping pipeline from the paper: PPMI motor assessments are aggregated into five domains, a BGMM configuration search selects the motor-state representation, posterior triage flags uncertain assignments, k=5 and k=8 solutions are reconciled, and imaging validation is performed with DaTSCAN and FreeSurfer MRI.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Motor-state heterogeneity</h3>\n<p>The selected five-state model includes moderate tremor, severe tremor, mild axial, severe axial, and moderate mixed motor-state families. Most assessments are high-confidence assignments, but the boundary cases are clinically important because they show where patient visits bridge state families rather than falling cleanly into one subtype.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/6274f/fig3_explainability_panels.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 82.5%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Model explainability and motor-domain separation' title='' src='/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/5a190/fig3_explainability_panels.png' srcset='/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/772e8/fig3_explainability_panels.png 200w,\n/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/e17e5/fig3_explainability_panels.png 400w,\n/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/5a190/fig3_explainability_panels.png 800w,\n/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/c1b63/fig3_explainability_panels.png 1200w,\n/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/29007/fig3_explainability_panels.png 1600w,\n/static/11cf3c67733b03d27af8374079f056c4/6274f/fig3_explainability_panels.png 2098w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 3.</strong> Paper figure showing motor-domain separation, effective component behavior across the configuration sweep, and temporal predictability between motor domains.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/00e09/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 70%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Posterior triage and hierarchical nesting' title='' src='/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/5a190/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png' srcset='/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/772e8/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png 200w,\n/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/e17e5/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png 400w,\n/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/5a190/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png 800w,\n/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/c1b63/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png 1200w,\n/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/29007/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png 1600w,\n/static/06f28fd824c890b192bdd05b552f198e/00e09/fig4_posterior_triage_nesting.png 1854w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 4.</strong> Posterior triage and hierarchical nesting. High-confidence textbook assignments dominate, while chimera assignments concentrate near specific motor-state boundaries. The five-state and eight-state solutions show strong correspondence.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Imaging validation</h3>\n<p>Motor-state assignments are associated with DaTSCAN striatal binding ratios in participants with matched imaging data, and with small-magnitude but significant FreeSurfer subcortical volume differences. The paper is careful about interpretation: these imaging results support complementary biological correlates, but they do not prove that the five states are fixed biological subtypes.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/2adcb/fig5_imaging_validation.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 66.5%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='DaTSCAN and FreeSurfer imaging validation' title='' src='/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/5a190/fig5_imaging_validation.png' srcset='/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/772e8/fig5_imaging_validation.png 200w,\n/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/e17e5/fig5_imaging_validation.png 400w,\n/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/5a190/fig5_imaging_validation.png 800w,\n/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/c1b63/fig5_imaging_validation.png 1200w,\n/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/29007/fig5_imaging_validation.png 1600w,\n/static/4666620769f7df1fa5b3e380deff6cf8/2adcb/fig5_imaging_validation.png 1984w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 5.</strong> Multimodal imaging validation from the paper. DaTSCAN SBR differs across motor states, and FreeSurfer-normalized subcortical volumes show small but FDR-significant state-associated effects.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Patient-level exemplars</h3>\n<p>The generated patient panels below illustrate how soft posterior profiles can map to different body-level motor expressions. These are concept figures, not individual clinical cases.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/ba6c0237738aa608f61cff45f7f4f032/62a6a/patient_a_tremor.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 125%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Tremor-weighted posterior patient exemplar' title='' src='/static/ba6c0237738aa608f61cff45f7f4f032/5a190/patient_a_tremor.png' srcset='/static/ba6c0237738aa608f61cff45f7f4f032/772e8/patient_a_tremor.png 200w,\n/static/ba6c0237738aa608f61cff45f7f4f032/e17e5/patient_a_tremor.png 400w,\n/static/ba6c0237738aa608f61cff45f7f4f032/5a190/patient_a_tremor.png 800w,\n/static/ba6c0237738aa608f61cff45f7f4f032/62a6a/patient_a_tremor.png 1122w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 6.</strong> Tremor-weighted posterior concept: upper-limb emphasis with lower axial and bulbar burden.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/ad6133fd13655a01ac6b97de0e2cd980/62a6a/patient_b_rigidity.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 125%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Rigidity-weighted posterior patient exemplar' title='' src='/static/ad6133fd13655a01ac6b97de0e2cd980/5a190/patient_b_rigidity.png' srcset='/static/ad6133fd13655a01ac6b97de0e2cd980/772e8/patient_b_rigidity.png 200w,\n/static/ad6133fd13655a01ac6b97de0e2cd980/e17e5/patient_b_rigidity.png 400w,\n/static/ad6133fd13655a01ac6b97de0e2cd980/5a190/patient_b_rigidity.png 800w,\n/static/ad6133fd13655a01ac6b97de0e2cd980/62a6a/patient_b_rigidity.png 1122w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 7.</strong> Rigidity-weighted posterior concept: stiffness and tone emphasis with moderate axial involvement.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/4921aef523c74872dc4c3dea1641039d/62a6a/patient_c_bradykinesia.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 125%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Bradykinesia-weighted posterior patient exemplar' title='' src='/static/4921aef523c74872dc4c3dea1641039d/5a190/patient_c_bradykinesia.png' srcset='/static/4921aef523c74872dc4c3dea1641039d/772e8/patient_c_bradykinesia.png 200w,\n/static/4921aef523c74872dc4c3dea1641039d/e17e5/patient_c_bradykinesia.png 400w,\n/static/4921aef523c74872dc4c3dea1641039d/5a190/patient_c_bradykinesia.png 800w,\n/static/4921aef523c74872dc4c3dea1641039d/62a6a/patient_c_bradykinesia.png 1122w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 8.</strong> Bradykinesia-weighted posterior concept: slowness, reduced movement amplitude, and distributed limb involvement.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/748f330f54e468d407a27b33d295204b/62a6a/patient_d_axial.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 125%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Axial-weighted posterior patient exemplar' title='' src='/static/748f330f54e468d407a27b33d295204b/5a190/patient_d_axial.png' srcset='/static/748f330f54e468d407a27b33d295204b/772e8/patient_d_axial.png 200w,\n/static/748f330f54e468d407a27b33d295204b/e17e5/patient_d_axial.png 400w,\n/static/748f330f54e468d407a27b33d295204b/5a190/patient_d_axial.png 800w,\n/static/748f330f54e468d407a27b33d295204b/62a6a/patient_d_axial.png 1122w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 9.</strong> Axial-weighted posterior concept: postural and gait involvement with tremor less prominent.</p>\n<p><span class='gatsby-resp-image-wrapper' style='position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 800px; '>\n      <a class='gatsby-resp-image-link' href='/static/601529c20afd97a5f989b700af20b003/62a6a/patient_e_bulbar.png' style='display: block' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>\n    <span class='gatsby-resp-image-background-image' style=\"padding-bottom: 125%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class='gatsby-resp-image-image' alt='Bulbar-weighted posterior patient exemplar' title='' src='/static/601529c20afd97a5f989b700af20b003/5a190/patient_e_bulbar.png' srcset='/static/601529c20afd97a5f989b700af20b003/772e8/patient_e_bulbar.png 200w,\n/static/601529c20afd97a5f989b700af20b003/e17e5/patient_e_bulbar.png 400w,\n/static/601529c20afd97a5f989b700af20b003/5a190/patient_e_bulbar.png 800w,\n/static/601529c20afd97a5f989b700af20b003/62a6a/patient_e_bulbar.png 1122w' sizes='(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px' style='width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;' loading='lazy' decoding='async'>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p><strong>Figure 10.</strong> Bulbar-weighted posterior concept: speech and swallowing emphasis with limited lower-limb burden.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Key findings</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A systematic 2,912-configuration BGMM search selected an effective five-state motor representation.</li>\n<li>Posterior triage assigned 99.5% of assessments to high-confidence textbook categories and 0.5% to intermediate-confidence chimera categories.</li>\n<li>Cross-granularity nesting between five- and eight-state views was strong, with Cramer's V = 0.945.</li>\n<li>DaTSCAN SBR differed across motor states in the imaging-matched cohort, including putamen and caudate associations.</li>\n<li>FreeSurfer MRI validation found small-magnitude subcortical volume differences, with 13 of 25 ROIs FDR-significant.</li>\n<li>Applying the fixed scaler and BGMM to BioFIND without refitting yielded 99.7% high-confidence assignments.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3>Interpretation and limits</h3>\n<p>The model should be read as a visit-level motor-state representation, not as proof of five stable biological patient subtypes. Repeated measures, possible severity confounding, and uncalibrated model posteriors limit the strength of causal or subtype claims. The value of the framework is that it makes assignment uncertainty visible while linking clinical motor-state structure to imaging-associated validation.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Citation</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bibtex\">@inproceedings{tirhekar2026posterioraware,\n  title     = {Posterior-Aware Motor Phenotyping with Multimodal Imaging Validation in Parkinson's Disease},\n  author    = {Tirhekar, Harsh Milind and Yadav, Priyanshi and Bajaj, Chandrajit},\n  booktitle = {Proceedings of the International Conference on Medical Image Computing and Computer Assisted Intervention},\n  year      = {2026}\n}\n</code></pre>","frontmatter":{"title":"Posterior-Aware Motor Phenotyping with Multimodal Imaging Validation in Parkinson's Disease","slug":"/projects/posterior-aware-pd-phenotyping"}}},"pageContext":{"id":"6e3030d9-1987-5e09-8e95-f3a65e8929a7","frontmatter__slug":"/projects/posterior-aware-pd-phenotyping","__params":{"frontmatter__slug":"projects"}}},"staticQueryHashes":["3431506307"],"slicesMap":{}}